Hello all,
FC8 is definitly amazing stuff, congratulations!!
I found some unexpected behaviour (on up2000+). Anybody seen these
issues too?:
1) sysrq-b (emergeny reboot) doesnt work (since at least kernel version
2.6.17). Still, all the other sysrq keys (emergency sync etc.) do work.
2) The 2.6.23 kernels (including the FC8 stock kernel) do not drop back
to SRM console at the end of shutdown, but just say "power off" before
hanging.
3) With 2.6.23 kernels "shutdown -r now" doesnt reboot, but hangs
shortly before dropping back to SRM. Looks like a side effect of issue
2)
4) The (modularized) FC8 xorg MGA driver dropped hw-accelerated xvideo
support, right? xine is really slow under FC8 on my matrox G400, much
slower than under AC2.

   Oliver



From Jay.Estabrook at hp.com  Tue Apr 15 21:11:34 2008
From: Jay.Estabrook at hp.com (Jay Estabrook)
Date: Tue, 15 Apr 2008 17:11:34 -0400
Subject: FC8 experience
In-Reply-To: <E3E4FC5CDA935240BCD2A8AE47B98DD4943EA2@ERLM862A.ww001.siemens.net>
References: <480364FC.206@hp.com>	<pwiqyjthkf.fsf@heppc02.nbi.dk><4804AA20.30200@hp.com>	<4804B31A.90808@linux-kernel.at>
	<E3E4FC5CDA935240BCD2A8AE47B98DD4943EA2@ERLM862A.ww001.siemens.net>
Message-ID: <48051A06.7020803@hp.com>

Answers:

1. sysrq-b

   sysrq-b is modified in arch/alpha/kernel/setup.c:setup_arch();
   it is changed to machine_halt instead of the default machine_restart

   I don't know the source of that patch; I don't remember doing it, or
   seeing it put in. Perhaps it's because Ctrl-Alt-Delete already exists
   to do a (graceful) reboot instead, though that's NOT a SYSRQ...

   Sorry, maybe someone else knows... ???

2 and 3. shutdown [-h|-r]

   "It works on my machine"... ;-}

   I've just done MANY shutdowns, both -h and -r, and they do the
   right things on all I can remember, except perhaps my UP1100.
   Notice anything different there? ;-}

   "Power off" is a message issued when going down a different path
   from the normal SRM halting; I can't think of why it'd do that on
   UP2000+ and not others... ???

4. HW-accel xvideo in modular MGA driver

   I don't know much about that one; looking at the changelog for that
   driver doesn't show anything pertinent, IMHO. You'll have to inquire
   elsewhere (freedesktop.org?).

   BTW, is it only on Alpha that you think the HW-accel xvideo is bust?

Thanks for the feedback!

--Jay++

